Article 1 Whoever violates laws and regulations on land administration, under any of the following circumstances, shall be deemed to have illegally occupied cultivated land, changed the purpose of the occupied cultivated land, and caused damage to cultivated land as prescribed in Article 342 of the Criminal Law:
(1) illegally occupying black soil land to carry out construction projects such as building houses, kilns, graves, or excavating lakes to create landscapes;
(2) illegally occupying black soil land to carry out activities such as sand excavation, quarrying, mining, or soil extraction;
(3) illegally occupying black soil land to discharge pollutants, dump waste, or otherwise cause severe pollution to the black soil land;
(4) other circumstances of illegally occupying black soil land, changing its purpose, and causing damage to the black soil land.
Where any act prescribed in the preceding paragraph is committed under any of the following circumstances, it shall be deemed to constitute “a relatively large quantity, causing extensive damage to farmland such as cultivated land and forestland” as prescribed in Article 342 of the Criminal Law:
(1) illegally occupying and destroying 3 mu or more of black soil land that is permanent basic farmland, or illegally occupying and destroying 6 mu or more of black soil land other than permanent basic farmland;
(2) illegally extracting 500 cubic meters or more of black soil from black soil land that is permanent basic farmland, or illegally extracting 1,000 cubic meters or more of black soil from black soil land other than permanent basic farmland;
(3) the quantity of black soil land illegally occupied and destroyed, or black soil illegally extracted, does not individually reach the standards specified in subparagraphs (1) and (2), but the total after conversion according to the proportion of the corresponding standards meets the standard;
(4) having received two or more administrative penalties for illegally occupying agricultural land within the past two years, and again illegally occupying and destroying black soil land, with the quantity reaching more than half of the standards specified in subparagraphs (1) to (3).

Article 6 Where a crime of damaging black soil resources is committed under any of the following circumstances, a severe punishment shall be imposed:
(1) continuing to commit the relevant act after the competent administrative department has issued an administrative decision ordering cessation of the illegal act and correction within a time limit;
(2) violently resisting or obstructing state functionaries from performing their duties according to law;
(3) bribing state functionaries.
Where an act under subparagraph (2) or (3) of the preceding paragraph also constitutes another crime such as the crime of disrupting public service, the crime of assaulting a police officer, or the crime of bribery, the offender shall be punished in accordance with the provisions on combined punishment for multiple crimes.
